- Move seeds, fertilisers, machinery, and harvested produce to safe storage where possible.
- Inspect existing drainage and clear it only when safe and permitted.
- Consider harvesting mature crops early when agronomically appropriate and safe.
- Prepare for the safe movement of livestock.
- Protect essential farm records and supplies.

Do not recommend dangerous actions such as entering rising floodwater, attempting unsafe river crossings, or approaching damaged electrical infrastructure.

Use reviewed agricultural guidance rather than generating unsupported pesticide, fertiliser, or crop-treatment instructions.

Allow farmers to mark checklist tasks as completed.

Explain that completing the checklist cannot guarantee that a crop will be saved.

